WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:03.780
Today we're going to talk about how to
prepare your life before starting at a

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:07.000
top law school, so stick around and get a
head start.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.980
Now, it's no secret that law

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:17.460
school is incredibly stressful. So many
lawyers I know say that law school was

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.510
the worst part of their entire lives. Now
it doesn't necessarily need to be that

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.810
way. You can do yourself a huge favor by

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:29.789
making your life in law school as easy
as possible, and here are the best ways

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:34.050
of getting your life in order so that
your life in law school is as good as it

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:38.280
can be. So here's my first piece of
advice: get an apartment that is as close

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:44.100
to campus as possible. I know it's
expensive it can't be helped. But if it

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.809
was between having roommates and living far away from campus, I would take the

00:00:48.809 --> 00:00:52.680
roommates. You're making an investment in law school, and if that means that you're

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.219
going to have to pay a little bit more
in rent to live closer to campus, I would

00:00:56.219 --> 00:00:59.039
recommend it.
Avoiding a commute can save you

00:00:59.039 --> 00:01:04.619
literally hours a day, and that's time
that you can use to either A) study more

00:01:04.619 --> 00:01:09.479
or B) relax. Both of which are
incredibly important when you get to law

00:01:09.479 --> 00:01:13.710
school. A friend of mine went to law
school in Los Angeles- he lived in West

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:20.040
LA, but he went to school in East LA. That
means that he had, in general, a 90-minute

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:26.880
commute each way - he lost three hours
every day he went to class. Now, law

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.020
school is a marathon, it's not a sprint.
You want to work a reasonable amount

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:36.570
every day. Adding an extra hour or two
because you're commuting is just a recipe

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:41.280
for disaster, so if you can do it, I
highly recommend living as close to

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:47.280
campus as possible. That brings me to my next tip: get the right technology when

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:52.170
you start. Now that means a new computer,
potentially a tablet, a laser printer-

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.799
these things will make your life so much
easier. We have an entire video dedicated

00:01:55.799 --> 00:02:00.180
to the tools that I wish I had when I
started law school. The technology has

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:05.340
gotten so great. There are a lot of good
tablets, a lot of good laptops, you get a

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:10.560
laptop with solid-state drive- one that
has a very long battery life you can

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.400
have laptops that last ten hours at a time. Not all law schools

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.150
have electrical outlets all over the
place, so you want a good laptop that

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:23.219
will last you a long time, and preferably
one with cloud storage so that you don't

00:02:23.219 --> 00:02:27.540
lose your important notes and your
outlines, because everyone has a horror

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:32.639
story where they lose that stuff and you
want the peace of mind. My next tip is

00:02:32.639 --> 00:02:36.750
related to the technology and that is: if
you have the time,

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:41.519
get your typing speed up. While law
school exams are not a brain dump in the

00:02:41.519 --> 00:02:46.950
same way that undergrad exams tend to be,
you still have a huge premium by being

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:51.480
able to type what you need to type as
quickly as possible. You can get more

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:55.439
points simply by virtue of being able to
type faster and more accurately than

00:02:55.439 --> 00:02:59.430
your peers. If you have some time in the
summer before law school, I would say

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:05.159
practice your typing- whether it's I
don't know Mavis Beacon or Mario Teaches

00:03:05.159 --> 00:03:10.139
Typing whatever the new typing software
is out there I would use it and get your

00:03:10.139 --> 00:03:13.859
typing speed up. I'd aim for a hundred
words per minute- you will be happy, it

00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:20.250
will serve you for the rest of your life  being able to type accurately. Next: get

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:25.530
your personal relationships in check.
It's a sad fact, but most couples break

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:29.549
up during law school. If your
relationship is going south, honestly

00:03:29.549 --> 00:03:34.979
it's better to end it now. Law school is
a time to focus, and if that means ending

00:03:34.979 --> 00:03:38.790
a bad relationship, do it before you get
to law school because you'll be happy

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:44.519
that you did. Next: deal with your health.
Law school is stressful, and your

00:03:44.519 --> 00:03:48.569
priorities are not going to be on
yourself, so in the summer before law

00:03:48.569 --> 00:03:53.310
school, deal with your health ahead of
time. Get a check-up, get a dentist

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:57.030
appointment, do it so that you're not
worried about that during your first

00:03:57.030 --> 00:04:02.219
year. There is no better way to derail
your finals than getting sick right

00:04:02.219 --> 00:04:08.129
before you take your first exam. Next:
mentally prepare. So, ahead of time I

00:04:08.129 --> 00:04:13.760
would say, do a little bit of research,
read "One L," watch the movie "The Paper Chase."

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:19.109
You're going to be putting in some long
hours, so I would recommend doing some

00:04:19.109 --> 00:04:23.130
research ahead of time to find out what
law school is going to be like. Now

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:27.180
obviously those are
dramatizations, they're not entirely

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:32.189
accurate. Both "One L" and "The Paper Chase"
take place in the 70s, and law school has

00:04:32.189 --> 00:04:38.759
changed, however it gives you a general
idea of what you're going to face. Next,

00:04:38.759 --> 00:04:44.819
and this is especially important: learn
how to hack law school. Doing well in law

00:04:44.819 --> 00:04:49.590
school, and especially on essay exams is
not a dark art, there is a science to it.

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:53.639
This is the number one missed
opportunity, learning how to take law

00:04:53.639 --> 00:04:58.740
school exams. Don't worry about learning
the law itself, there will be plenty of

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:04.650
time in law school to understand torts
and contracts and Civil Procedure. In law

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:08.909
school, your grades are determined
entirely based on your performance on

00:05:08.909 --> 00:05:14.310
your final exam. And what's worse, is that
it's graded on a curve so the professor

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:18.719
even if s/he wanted to give out all A's, is
limited and can only give out say five

00:05:18.719 --> 00:05:24.240
A's per class. Law school final exams are
almost always issue spotting exams, and

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:29.279
issue spotting exams are just like the
LSAT. There are strategies and tactics

00:05:29.279 --> 00:05:34.020
that can help you do better and the more
you practice the better you get at them.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:41.129
So it's so important to learn how to
take law school exams. At Legal Eagle, we

00:05:41.129 --> 00:05:46.169
offer an entire course on how to take
issue spotting exams. Additionally, use

00:05:46.169 --> 00:05:50.610
the time before law school to get your
resume, your letters of rec, and your

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:55.529
references in order. What nobody tells
you about law school is that you're

00:05:55.529 --> 00:06:00.719
going to apply for your summer jobs in
the middle of your 1L year. It can be

00:06:00.719 --> 00:06:04.740
incredibly stressful because you're
preparing for exams that you've never

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:09.419
seen before, you're learning law that you
have no frame of reference for, and in

00:06:09.419 --> 00:06:14.370
the middle of that you still have to
apply for jobs during the summer. So

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:19.199
those are the best ways to get your life
in order before you start law school. You

00:06:19.199 --> 00:06:23.879
can do yourself a huge favor by making
small tweaks that will make a huge

00:06:23.879 --> 00:06:28.800
difference in your law school career. Law
school is stressful enough, the last

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:33.180
thing you want to do is not prepare
ahead of time for things that could have

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:38.099
a huge impact during your law school
career. So remember, from everyone here at

00:06:38.099 --> 00:06:40.820
Legal Eagle, study smart through law school.

